A/A columns read `<verdict> <point> [<envelope>]`. THE BAND APPLIES TO THE POINT, NOT THE ENVELOPE:
the gate is |point-1| <= 0.02, plus an envelope that brackets 1.0 and is at most
0.60 wide. An envelope wider than the point band is NORMAL and is not a gate failure — it is a
bootstrap CI, and holding a CI inside +/-0.02 would be a different and far stricter
requirement than this protocol makes (frankentorch-strict-aa-gate-band-v8rpa).
Quote a lane only if both A/A gates say PASS, their point estimates are within +/-0.02 of 1.0, and parity is `match`. WIDE means the null's
CI exceeded 0.60 — the sample was too noisy to support ANY verdict, so the row is
undecidable rather than a win or a loss (frankentorch-8ieqm). Op-work ratios are NOT
comparable to the gauntlet's whole-step ratios, which include each lane's input rebuild.

